  "claim": "Affirmative action is the name of the disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture. The program Walter Henning was involved in is a form of that culture.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: Black Economic Empowerment (BEE) is a racially selective programme launched by the South African government to redress the inequalities of Apartheid by giving certain previously disadvantaged groups (Blacks, Coloureds, Indians, and Chinese) of South African citizens economic privileges previously not available to them under White rule.\nPage: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: It is a form of Affirmative action.\nPage: Affirmative action. Sentence: Affirmative action, also known as reservation in India and Nepal, positive action in the UK, and employment equity (in a narrower context) in Canada and South Africa, is the policy of favoring members of a disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture.\nPage: Walter Hennig. Sentence: He is known for his involvement in the Black Economic Empowerment programme and his experience in the mining industry.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: Black Economic Empowerment (BEE) is a racially selective programme launched by the South African government to redress the inequalities of Apartheid by giving certain previously disadvantaged groups (Blacks, Coloureds, Indians, and Chinese) of South African citizens economic privileges previously not available to them under White rule.\nPage: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: It is a form of Affirmative action.\nPage: Affirmative action. Sentence: Affirmative action, also known as reservation in India and Nepal, positive action in the UK, and employment equity (in a narrower context) in Canada and South Africa, is the policy of favoring members of a disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture.\nPage: Walter Hennig. Sentence: He is known for his involvement in the Black Economic Empowerment programme and his experience in the mining industry.",
