        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a42be139-c815-5229-bc1c-15deeea55b07",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Black Economic Empowerment, affirmative action\n- Places: South Africa, India, Nepal, United Kingdom, Canada\n- People: Walter Hennig\n- Topics: apartheid, mining industry\n\nFacts:\n- Black Economic Empowerment is a racially selective programme launched by the South African government to redress inequalities created by apartheid.\n- Black Economic Empowerment gives certain previously disadvantaged South African citizen groups, including Blacks, Coloureds, Indians, and Chinese, economic privileges that were not available under White rule.\n- Black Economic Empowerment is a form of affirmative action.\n- Affirmative action is a policy of favoring members of a disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture.\n- Affirmative action is also called reservation in India and Nepal, positive action in the United Kingdom, and, in a narrower context, employment equity in Canada and South Africa.\n- Walter Hennig is known for his involvement in the Black Economic Empowerment programme and for his experience in the mining industry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cdfc10b7-e43b-56a5-a9ac-ea53fedaf372",
        "text": "Page: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: Black Economic Empowerment (BEE) is a racially selective programme launched by the South African government to redress the inequalities of Apartheid by giving certain previously disadvantaged groups (Blacks, Coloureds, Indians, and Chinese) of South African citizens economic privileges previously not available to them under White rule.\nPage: Black Economic Empowerment. Sentence: It is a form of Affirmative action.\nPage: Affirmative action. Sentence: Affirmative action, also known as reservation in India and Nepal, positive action in the UK, and employment equity (in a narrower context) in Canada and South Africa, is the policy of favoring members of a disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture.\nPage: Walter Hennig. Sentence: He is known for his involvement in the Black Economic Empowerment programme and his experience in the mining industry.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
